      "facts": [
        "Compiles tool definitions into a single TypeScript definition file content. This generates type definitions for the given tools and their parameters."
      ],
      "title": "Shared/Core update: compile-tool-definitions",
      "summary": "Shared/Core changes across 1 file(s) (+69/−63).",
      "tags": [],
      "day": "2026-06-08",
      "month": "2026-06",
      "category": "Core",
      "significance": "minor",
      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "compileToolDefinitions accepts explicit tool list",
        "summary": "compileToolDefinitions in common/src/tools/compile-tool-definitions.ts now accepts an optional tools parameter, defaulting to getPublishedToolEntries(). Refactored to use a new ToolSchemaEntry interface, decoupling compilation from hardcoded publishedTools. Scope: Shared/Core. Detail: Enables tests or callers to compile definitions for specific schema subsets without modifying global constants.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:24:35.135Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the system generates its list of available tools for use, it now accepts an optional explicit list of tools to include, rather than always using the full published set. This lets developers running tests or specific workflows compile tool definitions for just the tools they need without altering the main shared list. The change is live in the shared code today. If you look, you'd see the generation step now takes a parameter that defaults to the usual full list, and a new structured entry holds each tool name and its parameter definition separately from the global constants.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "457b447afa2b",
        "at": "2026-09-17T20:32:00.621Z"
      },
